``dials.tof_integrate``: ``profile_1d_ibix`` and ``profile_3d_ibix`` take ``library.build=True`` to measure the peak shape on strong reflections and fit every reflection with the shape of the nearest of those held fixed (weak reflections in 3D at their predicted position). This replaces ``method=profile_1d_profilelib`` and ``method=profile_3d_profilelib``, which remain as deprecated aliases with their MANDI parameters. ``profile_3d_ibix`` now works in microseconds, as ``profile_1d_ibix`` does, with new fitting code: ``min_sigma``, ``max_sigma`` and ``init_sig_p`` are gone, and ``min_correlation`` and ``peak_height_fraction`` set when a reflection fitted on its own is accepted. Recommended parameters for MANDI are in each method's help. ``profile_1d_ic`` and ``profile_3d_ic`` fit with the same code and take ``library.build`` too, with the same acceptance options (``min_correlation``, ``peak_height_fraction``, and for 1D ``peak_tolerance`` and ``peak_height_smoothing``); ``profile_3d_ic`` now works in microseconds and ``init_sig_p`` is gone. ``profile_3d_gutmann`` fits with the same code too, now with the peak centroid fitted, the pulse integrated exactly over each time-of-flight bin, and the profile of Gutmann (2017) eq. (4); its eq. (6) as printed, which the previous code followed, lacks a 1/H6 in u and v. Its parameters are now those of ``profile_3d_ibix`` (``gradient_method`` is gone).
``dials.tof_integrate``: add ``overlaps.mode``. ``mask`` keeps reflections whose bounding boxes overlap, masking the voxels they share, instead of rejecting them all; ``deconvolve`` also fits clusters of overlapped reflections jointly in 3D against the profile library. ``overlaps.estimator=joint`` fits every reflection with the same 3D model, so that all profile-fitted intensities come from one estimator. Both need a profile method with ``library.build=True``.
